Make a struct implement `error` (an `Error() string` method), then let callers recover the fields with `errors.As`:

```go
type APIError struct { Status int; URL string }
func (e *APIError) Error() string { return fmt.Sprintf("%s -> %d", e.URL, e.Status) }

// caller:
var apiErr *APIError
if errors.As(err, &apiErr) && apiErr.Status == 429 {
    // back off and retry
}
```

Key points interviewers want: implement `error` on the pointer, optionally add `Unwrap()` to keep a wrapped cause in the chain, and use `errors.As` (not a type assertion) so it works through wrapping.
